@@ -3,3 +3,21 @@
 A small TypeScript library, with no runtime dependency, of building blocks for our services that store,
 exchange and update JSON: configuration files, API payloads and stored records. It is imported by the
 other projects of the team, so its behaviour must follow the published standards it implements.
+
+## JSON Pointer (RFC 6901)
+
+`resolvePointer(document, pointer)`, exported from `src/index.ts`, returns the value of `document` that
+`pointer` refers to.
+
+```ts
+resolvePointer({ foo: ["bar", "baz"] }, "/foo/1"); // "baz"
+resolvePointer({ "a/b": 1 }, "/a~1b"); // 1 (~1 is "/", ~0 is "~")
+resolvePointer({ a: 1 }, ""); // the whole document
+```
+
+It throws an `Error` when the pointer is not valid (it must be empty or start with `/`, and `~` must be
+followed by `0` or `1`) or when it does not resolve: a missing member, an array index that is out of
+range or not canonical (`01`, `-1`), the `-` token, or a step through a primitive. Only own members
+resolve, so `/toString` and `/__proto__` fail on a plain object.
+
+Run the tests with `npm test` (Node 22.18 or later, which runs the TypeScript sources directly).
diff --git a/src/index.ts b/src/index.ts
